title: DevShell Environment
status: proposed
created: 2026-11-07
author: adrian
context: "Litterbox provisions a sandbox from the project's `[[provision]]` steps (adrs/2026-11-05-sandbox-provisioning). Today the only kind is `command`, which runs inside the sandbox, and `CreateRequest` (crates/agentkit-litterbox/src/sandbox/contract.rs) carries no environment from the host and no store paths. A project that builds with Nix therefore has to run nix inside the sandbox, which the map excluded: with the daemon socket a confined command grew the host store and the daemon accepted builds outside the sandbox (maps/2026-10-31-nix-devshell-sandbox/evidence/T-018.md), and without it nothing evaluates. The same map established that a devShell can be prepared on the host instead: its exported variables plus the shell hook's additions and overrides reach a bubblewrap holder intact (T-011, T-016), and its store closure is a sufficient bind set (T-022). The contract as written has nowhere to carry either (T-023). This ADR adds a host step kind, `devshell`, and the effect vocabulary that lets a kind contribute something to a sandbox without the contract learning what Nix is: environment variables, read-only path grants and written files. Terminology is normative in crates/agentkit-litterbox/CONTEXT.md, upstream Nix terms are in .agentkit/tackle/prompts/nix/glossary.md, and the behaviours this specification relies on are verified in .agentkit/tackle/prompts/nix/PROMPT.md. Two questions decide the production shape and are not yet answered: whether a kind lives in the contract's closed `ProvisionKind` enum or in a registry outside it, and whether a backend reports kind support or effect support. This ADR specifies the design and produces a prototype that settles both against a real backend; it does not build the production implementation, which a follow-up ADR owns."
problem: "A project cannot express its devShell in configuration without either running nix inside the sandbox, which widens the host attack surface through the daemon socket, or hand-maintaining the environment variables and store paths that the flake already knows and that drift from it. The provisioning model has no way for a kind to contribute an environment, a path grant or a file, so adding one today means adding a devShell to the core contract, which couples every backend to one technology."
goals[9]:
  - "Add a devshell host step kind that prepares a devShell on the host and contributes effects to the sandbox."
  - "Define an effect vocabulary owned by the contract and independent of any technology."
  - "Produce the environment by difference under a sanitised baseline, from print-dev-env plus the shell hook."
  - "Carry the store closure as read-only grants, with the whole store as a machine option."
  - "Make the shell hook's bash functions available without re-running the hook."
  - "Persist effects with the sandbox, so later commands in later processes see the same environment."
  - "Refuse rather than realise, with a reason and a remedy the user can act on."
  - "Keep nix outside the sandbox: no daemon socket, no store write, no network."
  - "Settle the kind and effect boundary with a prototype before production types are committed."
nonGoals[10]:
  - "Running nix inside the sandbox."
  - "Realising the devShell; the user runs nix develop on the host first."
  - "Binding grants in a native backend; linux-bwrap-provider and darwin-sandbox-provider render them."
  - "Dynamic discovery or a plugin system for kinds; kinds are compiled in and registered in one place."
  - "The egress proxy (egress-proxy) and automatic backend selection (automatic-backend-selection)."
  - "Caching a prepared devShell across creates; it is derived from the store on each create."
  - "Migrating projects that hand-write environment variables to a devshell step."
  - "A Nix backend; a devShell is an environment, not a mechanism."
  - "The production implementation in Litterbox; a follow-up ADR consumes the prototype and implements it."
  - "Committing the prototype's type changes to the contract; the prototype ships nothing, and the follow-up decides the shape."
requirements[16]{id,title,slug,description}:
  FR-001,"Kind: DevShell Step",devshell-step,"A step of kind `devshell` names an installable: `identity`, `kind = devshell` and `installable`. Settings are validated when configuration loads; an unknown key or a missing installable fails naming the step identity and the kind. At most one devshell step may appear in one backend's sequence; a second is Misconfigured and names both identities."
  FR-002,"Arch: Kinds Are Compiled In",kinds-compiled-in,"Step kinds are compiled in and registered in one place, as backends are in the registry. A kind owns its settings, its validation and its execution. There is no discovery, no plugin path and no dynamic loading; adding a kind is a module and a registration line. A backend never learns a kind's name from the contract."
  FR-003,"Core: Effects",effects,"A host step contributes effects and nothing else. The vocabulary has three members: environment variables, read-only grants and written files. The contract defines these types and the request carries them in step order; it names no devShell, flake, nix, store or mechanism. A backend reports which effects it can honour; a request carrying one it cannot is refused before anything is created, naming the effect, the backend, the reason and the remedy, and is never silently dropped or approximated.\n\n{{mermaid: effects.mmd}}"
  FR-004,"Step: Host Placement",host-placement,"A devshell step is a host step: the orchestrator runs it during create, after resolution and the consent check and before the branch is created, so a failure leaves no branch, workspace or compute. It reads the project root, not the staged workspace, because the installable is relative to the checkout the user is in. It produces effects; it runs no sandbox and needs no backend.\n\n{{mermaid: create-sequence.mmd}}"
  FR-005,"Step: Differential Environment",differential-environment,"The environment is produced by difference, never by copying a session. The step takes every exported variable with a non-empty value from nix print-dev-env <installable> --json, then runs the shell hook once under a sanitised caller supplying only HOME and a minimal PATH, writing NUL-separated records to a file or spare descriptor rather than stdout, and takes the post-hook value of every variable that differs from the base or, where the base does not set it, from the sanitised caller. Additions and overrides are both taken. The step drops stdenv build-phase variables, the shell's own state, the evaluation artefact and the values the backend supplies. It never runs nix develop --command env, because that carries the caller's sockets and credentials."
  FR-006,"Step: Store Closure",store-closure,"The step derives the devShell's store closure with a host query over the output path print-dev-env reports, de-duplicated and absolute, and carries it as one read-only grant per path. The closure is the default store view. The contract sets no path ceiling and this ADR invents none: a backend that cannot honour a grant set validates it against its own limit before creating anything and refuses with that limit, the effect, the reason and the remedy. Whether a closure larger than this repository's 238 paths is bindable is untested, and that risk belongs to the backend ADRs that bind it."
  FR-007,"Config: Store View",store-view,"A machine-owned setting selects the store view: closure, the default, grants one path per closure member; whole grants the store root read-only instead. It lives in the local override as [nix] store, is ignored with the existing notice when the committed project file sets it, and applies to every devshell step on the machine. It exists because a closure can miss a path a build reaches at runtime, and the wide grant is the proven fallback."
  FR-008,"Step: Written File",written-file,"The shell hook's bash functions cannot be environment variables, so the step renders them from print-dev-env's bashFunctions into one written file. The backend places it inside the sandbox at a path it reports, read-only to the workload, and points BASH_ENV at it. A bash command then has the functions without naming them. Bash invoked as sh does not read BASH_ENV, so a command under another shell does not, and the report says so rather than implying the functions are global. A shell hook or a caller's shell rc that execs another shell is outside this guarantee and is recorded as a risk, not handled."
  FR-009,"Host: Readiness",host-readiness,"The kind reports host readiness, structured and without mutating anything: the nix executable is present and reports a version, flakes are enabled, the installable evaluates, and the devShell is valid in the store. Each check names the primitive, the reason and a remedy the user can run on the host. The same report is produced by the doctor and by create, from one implementation, and neither runs the preparation."
  FR-010,"Host: No Realisation",no-realisation,"The validity check is a store query, not a build: an unbuilt devShell is reported not valid and no output path is created. A step on an unrealised devShell fails create as Unavailable, naming the installable and the remedy of running nix develop on the host. print-dev-env may still copy the flake source to the store and may build a source derivation for a dirty tree; that is a store write, not a realisation of the devShell, and the reason and remedy say so rather than claiming nothing was written."
  FR-011,"Config: Consent",consent,"Preparing a devShell evaluates project code on the host, so it is consent-gated exactly as a command step is: the project's namespace is in allowed-projects, or allow-project-setup permits every project. A refusal is Denied, names the step identity and both settings, and no evaluation, query or backend call happens. Cloning a repository is never consent to evaluate its flake."
  FR-012,"Core: Persistence",persistence,"Effects persist with the sandbox, so every later command in every process sees the same environment, grants and written file: the backend stores them in its record payload and exec, inspect and delete read them from there. A prepared devShell is derived at create; a later change to the flake or the host does not reach a running sandbox, and creating again prepares it again. Delete removes the effects with the record."
  FR-013,"Core: Workspace Mapping",workspace-mapping,"The step records which environment values name the project root, such as CARGO_HOME, RUSTUP_HOME and the leading PATH entry, and the backend rewrites only those when it presents the workspace at a path other than the host's, as the contract requires. Store paths, including the NIX_ variables and toolchain paths, are never rewritten, because the store is granted at its own path. A value naming a host path outside the store and the workspace is reported as a host path and never granted."
  FR-014,"Core: Failure Classes",failure-classes,"A missing nix, disabled flakes, an installable that does not evaluate, or a devShell that is not valid in the store is Unavailable, each with the primitive, reason and remedy. An installable that evaluates to something without a devShell environment is Misconfigured. A shell hook that exits non-zero is Failed with the step identity and bounded output. A backend that cannot honour an effect is Unsupported. A refused step is Denied. These are the existing provisioning classes, not new ones."
  FR-015,"CLI: Doctor",doctor,"The doctor reports, without creating or mutating anything: the selected backend and its readiness; each devshell step with its identity, state, reason and remedy; the installable, whether it is valid in the store, the closure's path count, and the store view in force. It creates no sandbox, workspace, branch or store path, and it never prepares a devShell."
  FR-016,"Core: No Nix Inside",no-nix-inside,"The effects grant the sandbox no route to nix: no daemon socket, no store write and no network. The devShell's closure contains no nix executable, verified in this repository, and a nix binary found elsewhere could not reach the daemon because the socket is not granted and the network is unshared. A command that expects to evaluate or build fails as it would on a host without nix; the remedy is to run nix on the host and create again."
nonFunctional[9]{id,title,slug,description}:
  NFR-001,"Shared: No New Dependency",no-new-dependency,"The step spawns nix and reads its output with the standard library and the serde_json already in the tree. It adds no crate, no async runtime and no platform library."
  NFR-002,"Shared: Legible Unavailability",legible-unavailability,"Every failed check or refused effect names the primitive or effect, the reason and a remedy the user can act on. A bare failure is a defect, and each report is structured so a test asserts its fields."
  NFR-003,"Shared: Fail Closed",fail-closed,"No sandbox is created with a partial set of effects: a hook that fails, a variable that cannot be prepared, a closure that cannot be derived or an effect the backend cannot honour fails create and leaves nothing behind. The only way to run without the devShell environment is to remove the step from the sequence."
  NFR-004,"Arch: Host Boundary",host-boundary,"The devshell kind lives in its own module under src/provision/, reached by the orchestrator and never by a backend. A backend receives effects and cannot invoke nix. The boundary is declared in arch-lint.toml and a violation fails the build."
  NFR-005,"Shared: No Values On Surfaces",no-values-on-surfaces,"No CLI output, MCP response, log line or persisted provenance carries an environment value. A test asserts that rendered provenance and inspection do not contain a fixture secret."
  NFR-006,"Shared: Test Selection",test-selection,"Parsing and effect construction are unit-tested against recorded command output, with no nix and no network. Tests that need a real nix and a realised devShell are host tests, selected separately, and never build a derivation. Tests live in the module and are selectable by package and target."
  NFR-007,"Shared: Compatibility",compatibility,"A project with no devshell step behaves exactly as it does today; MCP tool names and arguments do not change; Docker continues to report the kind as unsupported rather than changing behaviour."
  NFR-008,"Shared: Documentation",documentation,"The configuration reference documents the devshell step, its installable, the store view and the consent it needs. The doctor output is documented with the other preflight output, and CONTEXT.md plus the nix capability prompt carry the vocabulary."
  NFR-009,"Shared: Prototype Is Not Shipped",prototype-not-shipped,"The prototype lives beside this ADR, under adrs/2026-11-07-devshell-environment/poc/, and no production module refers to it. Its findings are recorded beside it before the follow-up specification begins. A production type is not committed unless the findings support it."
acceptance[15]{id,title,slug,description}:
  AC-001,"Step: Differential Result",differential-result,"Against this repository's flake, the environment holds the base exported variables plus the hook's changes: the caller's RUSTFLAGS is absent from the result, PATH still leads with the devShell's CARGO_HOME entry, and SSH_AUTH_SOCK, BITWARDEN_SSH_AUTH_SOCK, DOCKER_HOST, DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS and WAYLAND_DISPLAY are absent. Build-phase variables and the shell's own state are dropped."
  AC-002,"Shared: Effects At Step Position",effects-at-position,"A recording backend receives the environment, grants and written file keyed to the devshell step's position: a command step before it sees the default environment, one after it sees the prepared environment, and a backend whose sequence does not name the step receives none of its effects."
  AC-003,"Step: Closure Equals Query",closure-equals-query,"The grants equal the de-duplicated output of the host closure query over the devShell's output path, one grant per path, and the count matches the query. With the store view whole, the grants are the store root alone. The doctor reports the count and the view."
  AC-004,"Host: Unrealised Refused",unrealised-refused,"With the devShell not valid in the store, create fails as Unavailable naming the installable and nix develop <installable>, the doctor reports the same, and the store gains no output path for it. A host test observes only the derivation being written."
  AC-005,"Host: No Nix Refused",no-nix-refused,"With no nix on PATH, readiness and create fail as Unavailable naming the primitive and the remedy, and the doctor reports it without creating anything."
  AC-006,"Config: Consent Gate",consent-gate,"A devshell step in a project outside allowed-projects is refused as Denied naming the identity and both settings and no nix process starts; the same project in allowed-projects prepares; allow-project-setup permits every project."
  AC-007,"Core: Persistence Across Processes",persistence-across-processes,"A sandbox created with a devshell step reports the same environment and provenance to a second process's exec and inspect, and delete removes the effects from the record."
  AC-008,"Step: Functions And Shells",functions-and-shells,"The written file defines the devShell's functions; a bash command in the sandbox resolves one without naming it; a command run as sh does not; and the report states that the functions are available to bash only."
  AC-009,"Core: No Socket Or Network Grant",no-socket-or-network,"The request carries no daemon socket, no store write and no network grant; its read-only grants are the closure members, the written file and the workspace, and a test asserts the grant set exactly."
  AC-010,"Config: Step Shape Refused",step-shape-refused,"A devshell step with an unknown key or a missing installable fails at load naming the key and the kind, and a second devshell step in one backend's sequence is refused naming both identities."
  AC-011,"CLI: Doctor Does Not Mutate",doctor-no-mutation,"Running the doctor on a project with a devshell step creates no sandbox, workspace or branch, and the store gains no path; a host test compares the store listing before and after."
  AC-012,"Shared: Provenance Carries No Value",provenance-no-value,"Inspection and MCP responses carry the step's identity, kind and changed variable names with change kinds, and no value; a fixture secret appears in no rendered output."
  AC-013,"Arch: Boundaries",boundaries,"The architecture lint denies a backend importing the provisioning module and denies the module importing a backend, and a negative fixture fails the build."
  AC-014,"Shared: Unsupported Backend",unsupported-backend,"With a devshell step in the project and a backend that does not report the effect set selected, create fails as Unsupported naming the backend, step and effect, the backend is never called, and the doctor reports the same."
  AC-015,"Prototype: Boundary Proven",boundary-proven,"The prototype declares a step whose kind is not named in the contract, and a real backend applies its environment, grants and written file without importing the kind. The findings record which of the two open questions the result settles, what it refutes, and what the follow-up ADR must decide."
edgeCases[10]{id,title,slug,description}:
  EC-001,"Step: Hook Fails",hook-fails,"A shell hook that exits non-zero fails create as Failed with the step identity and bounded output and leaves no branch, workspace or compute; the doctor reports the same reason."
  EC-002,"Step: Hook Prints",hook-prints,"A shell hook that prints to stdout does not corrupt the environment, because records go to a file or spare descriptor; a test with a banner-printing hook asserts every record is a well-formed assignment."
  EC-003,"Step: Not A DevShell",not-a-devshell,"An installable that evaluates but produces no devShell environment, such as a package rather than a shell, fails as Misconfigured naming the installable and what it produced."
  EC-004,"Host: Flakes Disabled",flakes-disabled,"With flakes disabled in the host's Nix configuration, readiness and create fail as Unavailable naming the experimental feature and the setting that enables it."
  EC-005,"Core: Backend Limit",backend-limit,"A backend that cannot grant the closure refuses the request with its own limit, the effect, the reason and the remedy, and the user can select the whole store view or a backend that can; no path is silently dropped."
  EC-006,"Core: Workspace Elsewhere",workspace-elsewhere,"When the workspace is presented at a path other than the project root, the recorded workspace-rooted values are rewritten and no store path is; a translation that would rewrite a store path is a defect and fails its test."
  EC-007,"Step: Shell Hook Execs A Shell",hook-execs-shell,"A shell hook or a caller's shell rc that execs another shell is outside the bash guarantee: the functions and BASH_ENV reach the first shell only. It is recorded as a risk, and no attempt is made to follow the exec."
  EC-008,"Host: Dirty Tree",dirty-tree,"A dirty Git tree changes the flake source, so print-dev-env may write a source path to the store and the closure may differ from a clean checkout's. A create that fails after this leaves that store write behind, and the report does not claim otherwise."
  EC-009,"Shared: Docker Selected",docker-selected,"With a devshell step in the project and Docker selected, create fails as Unsupported naming the backend, step and effect and Docker is never called; the doctor reports the same."
  EC-010,"Step: DevShell Changed After Create",devshell-changed,"A sandbox created before the flake changed keeps the effects it was created with; creating again prepares them again and may differ, and inspection names the preparation's origin so the difference is visible."
